{
	"_note": "Ichiro burns charcoal in Sakurazaka (the village's east part): a big quiet man who smells of smoke. Out early (6:30) to the bamboo grove and the woods north-east of the creek, where he cuts and hauls wood till noon; lunch at the Hanami teahouse (on its gravel, 12:00-12:45); stacking firewood by his house in the afternoon; home at 17:00, asleep from 20:00. Wet days he works in his earth-floored entry. Married to the farmer (married_ichiro, data/marriage.json) he lives at the farmhouse: by the kotatsu in the second room before 6:30 and from 17:00, his woods, lunch at the teahouse and his woodpile as before in between; on a wet day he walks over to split wood in his old earth-floored entry 7:00-17:00. On his birthday (fall 9, when the burning season starts) the axe rests: home in the morning, then a long sit on the teahouse gravel 10:00-14:00, home again after. His heart events: data/events/heart_ichiro.json (band 3), heart_ichiro_5.json (band 5). Gifts: hearty food, sweet potatoes, chestnuts; ores; he dislikes sweets and milk. Format: README.md, Villagers.",
